From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:08:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 154/274] Kernel preparation: WO, vocabulary heads and DSpark
 context KV declare their TileLang kernels

TileLangWOProjection lists WO-A's W8A16 kernels and WO-B's block-32 GEMMs as
calls and declares them from declare_kernels(), which its attention layer
calls; construction keeps only WO-B's scale words. WO-B takes WO-A's MXFP8
output, so its declaration (_declare_block32 with cast=False) warms no
per-token cast.

The packed LM head's method declares its projection from
declare_layer_kernels once the head is packed, since the kernels key on the
exponent base packing found; the weight hook packs and records the logits
dtype. A logits processor records the BF16 heads registered with it (the
DSpark Markov projection) and declares their kernels from declare_kernels().
The DSpark model declares its context KV projections.

